Implementation Plan: Per-Proc Toggles & Variable-Proc Sliders
Goal
Give each slotted proc its own control in the power InfoPanel: an on/off toggle (per-proc replaces the global category toggles as the default gate), plus a slider for variable procs — a stack slider (Might of the Tanker, 0–3 stacks) and an HP% slider (Reactive Defenses scaling resist, 3%→12.9%). State persists with the build. Sliders default to the expected-uptime contribution.

Design decisions (locked)
Per-proc is the default gate — global category toggles become a bulk convenience.
Persist with the build → state lives on the Build object, not transient uiStore.
Both slider types in v1 — stacks and HP-scaling.
Slider default = "Auto (expected uptime)" — a PPM→uptime→expected-stacks estimate; user can override to a discrete stack count or HP%.
Workstream 1 — Data descriptor (proc-data.ts)
Extend ProcEffect (line 67) so a proc self-describes its variable control:


export interface ProcEffect {
  // ...existing...
  /** Max concurrent stacks for a stacking buff proc (Might of the Tanker = 3). */
  maxStacks?: number;
  // `scaling: true` + `value`(floor) + `valueMax`(cap) already model HP-scaling.
}
