Behavior shift: MotT/Reactive resist currently contribute ~nothing; after this they add their expected value by default. That's the intended fix, but it will move existing builds' dashboard resistance — worth a changelog entry (changelog-manual.ts, which you have open).
Expected-stacks needs host-power recharge including slotted/global recharge; I'll source it the same way the Build Up proc path already does, so no new plumbing.
Keeping mode:'auto' as the absent-key default keeps procOverrides sparse and share-URLs small.
